hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1034","Ours is Muhammad bin Al-Ala’ Al-Hamdani, and Bishr bin Khalid Al-Askari, and this is the hadith of Muhammad bin Al-Ala. Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah Ibn Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed, but he did not do it, so he gave the salutation in the two rak’ahs, and Dhu al-Yadin said to him: Did you shorten the prayer or did you forget? He said: “The prayer was not short and I did not forget.” He said: “Is it as Dhu al-Yadin says?” So he stood up and prayed, then prostrated two prostrations. Abu Bakr said: This is news that was narrated on the authority of Abu Usama by someone other than Abu Kurayb, and this means Bishr bin Khalid."
